  "worked_solution": "To find the possible graph of the parabola, we need to determine two things:\n\n- The sign of the $y$-intercept.\n\n- The number of distinct real roots of the quadratic function.\n\nSince $c>0,$ the $y$-intercept must be positive. Moreover, since the discriminant $D>0,$ the quadratic function has two distinct real roots. So, it should intersect the $x$-axis twice.\n\nTherefore, of the given options, the only graph that satisfies both these conditions is the following:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14266874/assets/3247251e3ddf9bd0edf0f2ffce7d7c73b9a62b6b29012da7435dbeea0d2010bd.png)",
